 - \\(\\frac{11}{8} = 1.375\\).\n   - \\(\\frac{6}{16} = \\frac{3}{8} = 0.375\\).\n\n\n</partial_draft>","role":"user"},{"content":"Continue from the interruption. Output only the continuation. Do not restart the solution.","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"0a2d769bcff468d60906478f8c0eec42ef9f688f9a144fd4c551e0a30ea0c8b7"},"seconds":10.108384609222412,"seed":234070600971076160,"stop":"eos","text":"2. **Identify the greatest and the least member of the set:**\n   - The greatest member is \\(\\frac{11}{8} = 1.375\\).\n   - The least member is \\(\\frac{6}{16} = \\frac{3}{8} = 0.375\\).\n\n3. **Calculate the positive difference:**\n   - The positive difference between \\(\\frac{11}{8}\\) and \\(\\frac{3}{8}\\) is \\(\\frac{11}{8} - \\frac{3}{8} = \\frac{8}{8} = 1\\).\n\nThus, the positive difference between the greatest and the least member of the set is \\(\\boxed{1}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{1}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true,"retains_student_answer":false},"graded_text":"2. **Identify the greatest and the least member of the set:**\n   - The greatest member is \\(\\frac{11}{8} = 1.375\\).\n   - The least member is \\(\\frac{6}{16} = \\frac{3}{8} = 0.375\\).\n\n3. **Calculate the positive difference:**\n   - The positive difference between \\(\\frac{11}{8}\\) and \\(\\frac{3}{8}\\) is \\(\\frac{11}{8} - \\frac{3}{8} = \\frac{8}{8} = 1\\).\n\nThus, the positive difference between the greatest and the least member of the set is \\(\\boxed{1}\\).","id":"prealgebra:855"}
